A||||7||bilbo||EQUALIZER PICS.......||||1||
Z||000000||bilbo||01-21-2001||12:20 AM||||Anybody got any pics of their equalizers? I just got a full din equalizer and I'm looking for a place too put it in the car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||JetroGT||01-21-2001||06:04 AM||||If you don't mind not having the center vents anymore you could put it there. I saw it on a convertable. Lost the pic though...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-21-2001||07:12 AM||||Assuming that your EQ is about the same size as an aftermarket stereo, I don't think it would fit where the vents are.  Not enough depth unless you cut away part of the dash (unnoticable, but impossible to restore to original).  You might get creative and mount it where the overhead lights are.  You'd have to find another place for lights (lighted mirror, maybe?) and fabricate your own enclosure, but it would be trick.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||01-21-2001||10:27 AM||||You could put a single DIN receiver and a half-DIN EQ in the same space as the stock stereo, but that doesn't help you much. If you can return the EQ, you might try this or something like it:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-ajwRXkB2O7u/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=140&I=113KGC4032&o=M&a=0" TARGET=_blank>http://www.crutchfield.com/cgi-bin/S-ajwRXkB2O7u/ProdView.asp?s=0&c=3&g=140&I=113KGC4032&o=M&a=0</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||01-21-2001||11:19 AM||||What about in the center console in the "glove compartment"?  Might fit in there.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-21-2001||12:14 PM||||I have seen them in a housing above the console glove box facing forward, Under the passenger side dash, Mounted vertically between dash pod and radio console, Built in to the dash map pocket on the passenger side, Behind the seat near the top, and finally mounted on the side of the console were just the face shows (facing up) and the carpet covers the rest of it.<BR>These are just idea's I have seen. Personally the best looking was the one built into the dash on the passenger side map pocket. Not sure how they did it or how much room there is.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||01-21-2001||01:44 PM||||i've been considering all the options monkeyman mentioned plus a couple more. really want to try the deal where you take the face plate off and hard wire it to the reciever. if you could pull that off and put the radio behind the dash or just out of the way but still be able to get to it to put a cd/cassette in, then you could put the eq in the radio spot. <P>in another stereo thread right now someone named mblackwell showed a pioneer fh-m75 double din radio that he said is in his fiero. if thats possible and can be done pretty clean that may be the way to go.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierosound||01-21-2001||01:57 PM||||I've got an Audio Control 4-channel "set & forget" equalizer, as opposed to an in-dash unit.  I find you don't end up fiddling continuously, and your friends "can't play with it".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>This is mounted under the dash on the passenger side.  I get it "tuned" every spring using a RTA (Real Time Analyzer).  After that, I just use bass/treble controls on the deck for minor adjustments to those tunes that have too much or too little bass/treble.  Works great!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <P>||||reg||1
